00:17:43,740 --> 00:17:46,937
I'll never forget watching my fellow crew

264
00:17:47,020 --> 00:17:49,637
mate as he was killed
right in front of me.

265
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:53,500
I will not accept help from you
we will stop the ship ourselves!

266
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:03,056
Kite, what are you going to do, Kite?

267
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:06,060
Quit bugging me, I know.

268
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:09,817
The time has come for me to pay
the price for what I've done.

269
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:12,540
Only 4,500 yards left till the deadline.

270
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:22,100
4,000 yards remaining.

271
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,180
Okay, that's it.

272
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:32,406
All right, let's get it open.

273
00:18:38,540 --> 00:18:40,300
3,500 yards.

274
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:42,260
3,000.

275
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:44,753
What's with this place?

276
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:46,488
It's like a cellar in here.

277
00:18:46,860 --> 00:18:47,840
2,500.

278
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:50,380
It's way over there.

279
00:18:56,060 --> 00:18:58,620
It isn't working, dammit! It won't punch!

280
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:02,437
There just isn't any way we can
get through this mass of pipes!

281
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:03,480
1,800.

282
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:06,480
Come on. It's hopeless.

283
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:07,777
There's nothing we can do.

284
00:19:07,860 --> 00:19:08,977
We're not gonna make it.

285
00:19:09,060 --> 00:19:10,840
Calm down. There's a way.

286
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:12,080
There's gotta be.

287
00:19:47,140 --> 00:19:49,817
The emergency stop system
has been activated, sir.

288
00:19:49,900 --> 00:19:51,724
How many yards do we have left?

289
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:52,930
800!

290
00:19:54,720 --> 00:19:56,740
We're just going too fast!

291
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:57,980
It's too late!

292
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:33,780
Thanks to Mr.

293
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:36,920
Nasty's selfless act of
heroism, we were all saved.

294
00:20:37,300 --> 00:20:38,280
Neon did that?

295
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:40,640
Now don't get the wrong idea.

296
00:20:40,940 --> 00:20:42,820
I just paid off my wager.

297
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:46,080
The next time we meet,
it's no holds barred.

298
00:20:46,300 --> 00:20:48,820
I'll take that life of yours. Count on it.

299
00:20:52,820 --> 00:20:56,173
That smug jerk laid it on us
real thick all the way home.

300
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:22,697
So, on the first evening of Pebble,

301
00:21:22,780 --> 00:21:29,260
From somewhere out of nowhere
drops upon the dreaming world

302
00:21:30,940 --> 00:21:31,770
Sooooooooooo?

303
00:21:31,853 --> 00:21:32,817
That song. Yeah?

304
00:21:32,900 --> 00:21:35,057
I know it's an old song, but I like it.

305
00:21:35,140 --> 00:21:36,940
It's a good song, so shut up.

306
00:21:37,180 --> 00:21:39,920
Oh, yeah, right. It's a good song.

307
00:21:45,860 --> 00:21:50,880
From somewhere out of nowhere
drops upon the dreaming world

308
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:56,300
It's the same song that she loved.

309
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:14,957
Hey, will you stop it?

310
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:16,275
You're making me cry!

311
00:22:16,840 --> 00:22:17,670
AHH!!

312
00:22:17,860 --> 00:22:20,137
What made up front of me, a-fif-fuckhead!

313
00:22:20,220 --> 00:22:21,457
Oh, I meant you were hearing it!

314
00:22:21,540 --> 00:22:23,187
Shut up, you flaky show-off!

315
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:24,927
What kind of flaky show-off?

316
00:22:25,100 --> 00:22:27,453
That's why you're not gonna be anything!

317
00:22:27,680 --> 00:22:29,092
Let's take care of them.

318
00:24:06,120 --> 00:24:08,320
I met a lone man in the desert.

319
00:24:08,420 --> 00:24:12,140
a traveling priest, Nicholas D. Wolfwood.

320
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:15,715
He smiled, and then he told
me that I'm a troubled man.

321
00:24:16,500 --> 00:24:21,029
Faced with his all-seeing smile, there
was nothing I could say in my defense.

322
00:24:21,180 --> 00:24:23,886
Did I meet this man
because I was destined to?

323
00:24:24,620 --> 00:24:27,560
Or was it simply by a small gist of God?

324
00:24:28,320 --> 00:24:30,026
The man's name is Nicholas D.

325
00:24:30,160 --> 00:24:33,042
Wolfwood, a traveling
priest I met in the desert.
